<title>INDIA: India's SBI 96/97 1st half net rises.</title>
<headline>India's SBI 96/97 1st half net rises.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-11-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to September 30, 1996</p>
<p>	     (in million rupees unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit	    6,408.0   vs     2,304.0</p>
<p>INCOME</p>
<p>    Interest earned    74,143.4   vs    59,705.9</p>
<p>    Other income	 11,614.3   vs    10,825.2</p>
<p>    Total income	 85,757.7   vs    70,531.1</p>
<p>EXPENDITURE</p>
<p>    Interest expended  47,341.0   vs    36,808.9</p>
<p>    Operating expense  21,347.6   vs    20,392.1</p>
<p>Provisions &amp;</p>
<p>     contingencies     10,661.1   vs    11,026.1</p>
<p>    Total		  79,349.7   vs    68,227.1</p>
<p>Note: State-run State Bank of India (SBI) is India's largest commercial bank.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
</text>
